    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "yeah, the goal is basically to reduce the risk of a single point of failure. the current centralized setup is seen as a vulnerability for cyber attacks or a cascading failure if your core logic hits a snag. the new protocol is meant to make the grid more resilient by distributing control. do you think the latency you mentioned is a dealbreaker for the transition?",
